  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 143 AM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nA more active weather pattern is on the way beginning this weekend \nas models bring an upper trough close to our region. Abundant \nmoisture coupled with several shortwaves moving through the flow \naloft and upslope flow at the surface yield increasing shower/storm \nchances (20-60%) areawide this weekend into next week. Lower heights \nassociated with the aforementioned trough and increasing cloud cover \nalso allow for temperatures to gradually cool each day, potentially \ncooling most into the 80s to low 90s by early next week due to a \ncold front. However, it should be noted that confidence is currently \nlow due to large spread in the temperature data among the ensembles. \nTemperatures next week will highly depend on the positioning of the \ntrough/cold front and cloud cover/rainfall.\n  \nGreening",
